ca-06017-bos-matter-41388.title:
District Attorney's Office recommending the Board: 
1) Receive and file the Law Enforcement Panel’s approval for the District Attorney’s use of 15% Asset Forfeiture Funds to support the following: a $10,000 contribution to the California District Attorneys Association (CDAA) Drug-Prosecution Training Initiative; a $15,000 contribution to Big Brothers Big Sisters (BBBS) for community outreach programs; a $2,000 contribution to the annual community Drug Store Project; $23,000 for multimedia production services promoting fentanyl-use deterrence; and $10,000 for community advertising on the negative impacts of drug use;
2) Find that the proposed uses provide a valuable public benefit by supporting programs designed to combat drug abuse and divert gang activity;
3) Adopt and authorize the Chair to sign Resolution 168-2026, approving the above-listed contributions to CDAA, BBBS, and the Drug Store Project; and
4) Approve and authorize the Chair to sign the associated Fiscal Year 2026-2027 budget transfer increasing revenue and appropriations within the District Attorney’s General Fund by $60,000. (4/5 vote required)
 
FUNDING: District Attorney 15% Asset Forfeiture Fund.

